# credgate + latch -- CARRIES A RETRACTION. The derived and latch arms never
# consulted the creature's context index.
# 2026-09-19. verify PASS, hash ad96f882becbee92.
#
# THE TELL: the latch arm came back BIT-IDENTICAL to derived -- retention
# 0.461 +/- 0.385 and agreement 0.720 in both. Two different masking rules cannot
# agree to three decimals unless both are constant.
#
# THE CAUSE: dna/default.toml has context_slots = 0. There is no context module,
# so Network::active_context() returns 0 on every tick:
#   derived: upper = (active_context() == 0) = TRUE always
#   latch:   upper = (latched_ctx == 0)      = TRUE always, the latch never fires
# Both arms are one fixed policy: ALWAYS MASK TO A'S HALF.
#
# AND 0.720 IS NOT AN INDEX ACCURACY. agreement counts upper == want, and with
# upper constantly TRUE it reduces to the fraction of trials where want is TRUE:
# the teach phase (60%) plus the after phase (12%) = EXACTLY 0.720. A trial-ratio.
# The keep arms read 1.000 for the same reason -- their second lesson also targets
# 320, so want is TRUE in every phase.
#
# WITHDRAWN: 'the index carries which lesson is live at 0.720 vs a 0.477 coin
# flip'; 'it delivers 0.387 of the 0.440 its accuracy predicts'; and 'this is an
# accuracy problem with a measured conversion rate'. None of those were measured.
#
# WHAT SURVIVES:
#   - the ORACLE removes the wipe: -0.041 -> 1.254, +1.295 (+4.8 SE);
#   - a COIN FLIP does not: -2.285 +/- 2.556 (-0.9 SE), so it is credit
#     assignment and not merely halving the write;
#   - a FIXED CONTEXT-FREE policy ('always mask to A's half') buys +0.501 +/-
#     0.439 (+1.1 SE) -- suggestive, and interesting because it needs no context
#     signal at all;
#   - the mask costs learning rate: err_taught 0.9439 -> 1.0266.
#
# THE INDEX CANNOT BE TESTED ON THIS GENOME. A context genome must come from
# tools/ctxgenome.sh, and it FAILS calibrate (somato 4.16 Hz vs a 4.56 target,
# -0.40). Fixing that is the prerequisite for the whole gating question.

